# `python -m compileall -q src` is one of this repository's gates, so running the
# gates writes bytecode into the tree. None of it belongs in a commit.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Scratch files reviewers and agents leave in the repo root.
factory-testbed-*.txt
factory-testbed-*.golden

# Per-item agent artifacts. These live in the build worktree and must never be
# committed: a blanket `git add -A` in a worktree that holds them sweeps them
# into the PR. That has now happened twice in this repo's history - see the
# commit "Remove two reviewer scratch files that a blanket 'git add -A' swept
# in", and again in #90. Ignoring them makes the mistake impossible rather than
# something the next person has to remember.
PLAN.md
AGENT-REPORT.md
ISSUE_CORRECTIONS.txt
ISSUE_BODY.md
PR_BODY.md
